'''Legeluga''' is a [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] that can be obtained at an extremely low chance when playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Tales of the Nekoluga]] event. It was added in [[Version 8.3 Update|Version 8.3]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 461
|rarity = LR
|name1 = Legeluga
|name2 = Legelan Pasalan
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Legelan Pasalan''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Legelan Pasalan has a few main points of interest, one of which is its [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]]. Being able to outrange most [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]], it works rather well against them. It will stay at a safe range from a significant amount of wave attackers whilst dishing out good damage, unlike most other rushers who will get sniped on their way.

Another point of interest is its DPS. It is very impressive for its range, over 12k in fact. It can be used in places for short burst of damage alongside other rushers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. It also has lots of knockbacks that enables the unit to skip its backswing and deal even more damage.

However, it isn't without its weaknesses. Legelan Pasalan's range is quite mediocre, standing at just 300, and while other stronger rushers fail in this aspect, they make it up with much higher overall damage. Its 50k health, 124s cooldown (many rusher units of the same caliber like Awakened Bahamut, [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]], [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]] and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] have cooldowns around 90 seconds or less) are less than stellar, and Knockback/Warp Immunity actively hinder this unit since it cannot abuse these effects to reset its backswing. Because of this, take caution and send it out only when the time is right. Its one saving grace as a rusher is that it does not move again after attacking until its backswing is over. Use this knowledge carefully, as you wouldn't want it to not move when you want it to, or for it to move before you're ready.

